      "history_summaries": [
        "Round 1: Fixed barrel shifter cascade bug (rotation_correctness). Error: dut_bug. Root cause: stages 2-5 read from tmp0 (inrReg) instead of the previous stage's output, breaking composable rotation. Changed Cat(tmp0(...), tmp0(...)) to Cat(tmp1(...), tmp1(...)) in stage 2 (line 47), Cat(tmp2(...), tmp2(...)) in stage 3 (line 54), Cat(tmp3(...), tmp3(...)) in stage 4 (line 61), Cat(tmp4(...), tmp4(...)) in stage 5 (line 68). This fixes the cascade so each stage rotates the previous stage's output, composing all active amount bits. All other logic and all three assertion labels (rotation_correctness, spin_mode_update, load_mode_update) are preserved unchanged.",
        "Round 2: Fixed uninitialized RegNext registers causing load_mode_update and spin_mode_update assertion failures. Error type: dut_bug. Root cause: `dinDelayed = RegNext(io.din)` and `doutRegDelayed = RegNext(doutReg)` lacked explicit reset values, allowing the formal solver to pick arbitrary initial values (e.g., 0x80000000 for dinDelayed) that mismatch the properly-reset inrReg (0x00000000) at cycle 0. The fix adds `0.U(32.W)` as reset value to both RegNext calls on lines ~98 and ~94: `RegNext(io.din, 0.U(32.W))` and `RegNext(doutReg, 0.U(32.W))`. This ensures that after reset all registers (inrReg, dinDelayed, doutRegDelayed) agree on value 0, so the load_mode_update and spin_mode_update assertions hold at cycle 0 and thereafter. All three assertion labels (rotation_correctness, spin_mode_update, load_mode_update) are preserved unchanged.",
        "Round 3: Fixed load_mode_update assertion timing error. Error type: assertion_error. Root cause: assertImpliesDelay(!splReg, inrReg === dinDelayed, 1, ...) used delay=1, checking 1 cycle too late. By cycle T+1, inrReg may be overwritten by spin-mode feedback (inrReg := doutReg) and dinDelayed captures io.din(T) which no longer matches inrReg(T+1). Fix: changed delay=1 to delay=0 and replaced dinDelayed with io.din, so the check is combinational in the same cycle where !splReg is true and inrReg := io.din takes effect. Removed now-unused dinDelayed val. spin_mode_update (homologous structure) is preserved with delay=1 because it checks inrReg === doutRegDelayed where doutReg is a register whose captured value remains valid one cycle later, unlike the unregistered io.din. Target assertion label 'load_mode_update' preserved unchanged."
      ],
